</div>



<div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Accounting for creditor concessions to a distressed debtor</div><div class="principle">ASBE No. 12 governs the RECOGNITION and MEASUREMENT of DEBT RESTRUCTURING — WHERE a CREDITOR makes CONCESSIONS to a DEBTOR EXPERIENCING FINANCIAL difficulty (e.g. EXTENDING repayment TERMS, reducing PRINCIPAL or INTEREST, or ACCEPTING non-cash ASSETS or EQUITY in SETTLEMENT). This STANDARD'S HISTORY includes a GENUINELY significant EVOLUTION in HOW resulting GAINS are RECOGNISED (Section 5).</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope — Creditor Concessions to a Financially Distressed Debtor</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Both the debtor's and the creditor's own accounting</div><div class="principle">This Standard applies to BOTH the DEBTOR and the CREDITOR involved in a QUALIFYING debt RESTRUCTURING — WHERE the DEBTOR is EXPERIENCING genuine FINANCIAL difficulty, and the CREDITOR agrees to MAKE a CONCESSION it WOULD NOT otherwise MAKE, absent that DIFFICULTY.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Forms of Debt Restructuring</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Several possible restructuring mechanisms</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Form</span><span>Description</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Settlement with cash</span><span>Debtor pays a REDUCED cash amount to fully SETTLE the debt</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Settlement with non-cash assets</span><span>Debtor TRANSFERS assets (e.g. INVENTORY, fixed ASSETS) in SETTLEMENT of the debt</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Debt-to-equity swap</span><span>Debtor ISSUES equity INSTRUMENTS to the CREDITOR in SETTLEMENT of the debt</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Modification of terms</span><span>Extending the REPAYMENT period, REDUCING the interest RATE, or WAIVING accrued INTEREST</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>The Debtor's Perspective — Recognising a Restructuring Gain</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">The difference between the debt extinguished and the consideration given</div><div class="text-supporting">FROM the DEBTOR'S perspective, a GAIN on DEBT restructuring is RECOGNISED for the DIFFERENCE BETWEEN the CARRYING amount of the DEBT extinguished and the FAIR VALUE of the CONSIDERATION given (CASH paid, non-CASH assets TRANSFERRED, or EQUITY instruments ISSUED) — REFLECTING the ECONOMIC benefit the DEBTOR receives FROM the creditor's CONCESSION.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>THE HISTORICAL SHIFT — From Capital Reserve to Profit or Loss</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">A significant change introduced by the 2006 ASBE reform</div><div class="text-supporting">UNDER the OLDER, PRE-2006 Chinese accounting RULES, a GAIN arising from DEBT restructuring was CREDITED DIRECTLY to CAPITAL RESERVE — a COMPONENT of OWNERS' equity — RATHER than FLOWING through the INCOME STATEMENT at ALL. The 2006 ASBE OVERHAUL CHANGED this TREATMENT: restructuring GAINS are NOW recognised DIRECTLY in PROFIT or LOSS — a GENUINELY significant HISTORICAL evolution, ALIGNING China's approach with the GENERAL international TREATMENT of debt EXTINGUISHMENT gains (e.g. under IFRS 9).</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Why the 2006 Reform Moved Gains Into Profit or Loss</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Reflecting the reform's broader convergence objective</div><div class="text-supporting">The OLDER capital-RESERVE treatment REFLECTED a MORE CONSERVATIVE, PRUDENCE-oriented APPROACH — AVOIDING the POTENTIAL for EARNINGS management THROUGH engineered debt RESTRUCTURINGS that COULD otherwise BOOST reported PROFIT. The 2006 REFORM'S broader CONVERGENCE objective (see the COMPANION overview discussion EARLIER in this SERIES) PRIORITISED aligning China's TREATMENT with INTERNATIONAL practice OVER retaining this OLDER, more CONSERVATIVE convention — a GENUINELY notable ILLUSTRATION of HOW the 2006 reform SHIFTED specific, LONG-STANDING Chinese accounting CONVENTIONS toward international ALIGNMENT.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>The Creditor's Perspective — Recognising a Restructuring Loss</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Adjusting the receivable, recognising a corresponding loss</div><div class="text-supporting">FROM the CREDITOR'S perspective, the RECEIVABLE is ADJUSTED to REFLECT the CONCESSION granted, WITH a CORRESPONDING loss RECOGNISED in PROFIT or LOSS for the DIFFERENCE between the RECEIVABLE'S carrying AMOUNT and the FAIR value of WHATEVER consideration is ULTIMATELY received.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Debt-to-Equity Swaps</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Equity issued measured at fair value</div><div class="text-supporting">WHERE a DEBTOR issues EQUITY instruments to the CREDITOR in SETTLEMENT of a DEBT, the EQUITY instruments are MEASURED at FAIR value — with the DIFFERENCE between this FAIR value and the CARRYING amount of the DEBT extinguished RECOGNISED as a GAIN (for the DEBTOR) or LOSS (for the CREDITOR), CONSISTENT with the GENERAL debt RESTRUCTURING framework.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Worked Example — a Debtor's Gain on Debt Forgiveness</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Recognising a gain directly in profit or loss</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A creditor accepting a reduced cash settlement</div><div class="wk-body">A financially distressed debtor owes RMB 10,000,000 to a creditor. The creditor agrees to accept a cash payment of RMB 7,500,000 in full and final settlement of the debt.</div><div class="wk-answer">The DEBTOR recognises a GAIN on DEBT restructuring of RMB 10,000,000 − RMB 7,500,000 = <strong>RMB 2,500,000</strong>, recognised DIRECTLY in PROFIT or LOSS under the CURRENT (post-2006) treatment — WHEREAS, under the OLDER pre-2006 RULES, this SAME gain would have been CREDITED directly to CAPITAL reserve WITHIN equity instead.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Worked Example — a Debt-to-Equity Swap</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Measuring the equity issued at fair value</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: Converting debt into shares</div><div class="wk-body">A debtor owes RMB 20,000,000 to a creditor. As part of a restructuring, the debtor issues new shares with a fair value of RMB 15,000,000 in full settlement of the debt.</div><div class="wk-answer">The DEBTOR recognises the NEW shares WITHIN equity at their FAIR value of RMB 15,000,000, and a GAIN on DEBT restructuring of RMB 20,000,000 − RMB 15,000,000 = <strong>RMB 5,000,000</strong>, recognised in PROFIT or LOSS.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What ASBE No. 12 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Form of debt restructuring undertaken (cash, non-cash assets, equity, or modified terms)</span><span>Gain or loss recognised on the restructuring, and its basis for measurement</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
<div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Whether the debtor is genuinely experiencing financial difficulty, qualifying the transaction as a restructuring</span></div></div>
<div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Fair value of non-cash assets or equity instruments transferred in settlement</span></div></div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Relationship to IFRS 9</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — ASBE 12 vs IFRS 9's debt extinguishment provisions</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">ASBE 12 (current)</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IFRS 9</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Gain recognition</span><span>Profit or loss</span><span>Profit or loss — converged (post-2006)</span></div>
</div>
<div class="note">CONVERGED SINCE the 2006 REFORM — the MOST interesting FEATURE of this STANDARD today is ITS OWN historical EVOLUTION, RATHER than any ONGOING, current-day DIVERGENCE.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every debt restructuring event lands</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Debtor's gain on restructuring</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge bp">IS</span></span><span>Recognised directly in profit or loss</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Creditor's loss on restructuring</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge bp">IS</span></span><span>Recognised as a reduction to the receivable</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASBE No. 22</span><span>Recognition and Measurement of Financial Instruments — supplies the general financial liability derecognition framework this Standard's debtor treatment parallels</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s16"><span class="num">16</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2">
<div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Debt restructuring (债务重组)</div><div class="glossary-def">A creditor's concession to a debtor experiencing genuine financial difficulty, taking the form of reduced cash settlement, non-cash asset transfer, equity issuance, or modified terms.</div></div>
<div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Debt-to-equity swap</div><div class="glossary-def">A restructuring in which a debtor issues equity instruments, measured at fair value, in full or partial settlement of a debt.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Chinese GAAP / ASBE terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><div class="litem"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (资产负债表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bp">IS</span> Income Statement (利润表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bo">SCOE</span> Statement of Changes in Owners' Equity (所有者权益变动表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bc">CFS</span> Cash Flow Statement (现金流量表)</div></div></div>


</div>
  </div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.asbe12 || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>
